id: pm-v7e337
title: "MCP subscriptions and transports: subscriptions/listen, request-scoped streams, Streamable HTTP headers, retry semantics, and stdio parity"
description: "Replace connection-session and legacy subscription behavior with the 2026-07-28 long-lived listen request, request-scoped notifications, required headers, and explicit broken-stream retry semantics."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[8]: "area:mcp",cancellation,headers,progress,stdio,streamable-http,streaming,subscriptions
created_at: "2026-08-25T05:09:03.758Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T05:50:35.874Z"
deadline: "2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 840
acceptance_criteria: "subscriptions/listen supports every specified notification type and tags notifications with the negotiated subscription id; Legacy HTTP GET, resources/subscribe, resources/unsubscribe, session headers, Last-Event-ID, SSE event ids, and redelivery semantics are absent from the canonical path; Progress and logging notifications remain request-scoped and cannot leak across concurrent requests; STDIO and Streamable HTTP pass equivalent tool, resource, prompt, cancellation, backpressure, disconnect, and retry cases; Mcp-Method, Mcp-Name, and x-mcp-header behavior is schema-derived, validated, and covered against injection and mismatch"
goal: Transport parity without protocol sessions
objective: "Provide standards-correct stdio and Streamable HTTP operation for request responses, opted-in changes, progress, cancellation, and disconnect recovery"
value: Hosts can deploy pm locally or remotely with one transport-neutral state model
why_now: "The revision removes HTTP GET, MCP session IDs, resource subscribe methods, SSE resumability, and Last-Event-ID while adding subscriptions/listen and required POST headers"
parent: pm-rs9vry
risk: critical
confidence: medium
